meta {
  name: Upload Document
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/ingest
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
  ~X-Version-Tag: qwen3-baseline
}

body:multipart-form {
  file: @file(./samples/sample.txt)
  department: medical
}

docs {
  # POST /api/v1/ingest

  Upload a document and **enqueue a Temporal workflow** for ingestion.
  Returns `202 Accepted` with the new `job_id` (UUID). The workflow id
  is derivable as `ingest-{job_id}`.

  ## Flow
  1. File body is read into memory.
  2. Object stored in MinIO at `s3://kb-uploads/{job_id}/{filename}`.
  3. Row inserted into Postgres `documents` (status=`pending`).
  4. `DocumentIngestWorkflow.run(IngestParams(doc_id, s3_uri))` started
     on task queue `kb-ingest`.
  5. Response returns immediately — poll `GET /api/v1/ingest/{job_id}`
     for progress.

  ## Form parameters
  - **file** *(required)* — the document. Supported: PDF, DOCX, PPTX,
    TXT, MD, EML (via LlamaIndex `SimpleDirectoryReader`).
  - **department** *(optional)* — free-form tenant tag; populates
    `documents.department` for filtering at search time.

  ## Headers
  - **X-API-Key** *(required)* — one of the keys in the `API_KEYS` env.
  - **X-Version-Tag** *(optional, disabled by default)* — analytics
    label for this ingest; written to `ingest_metrics.version_tag` and
    Temporal search attrs. Falls back to `ANALYTICS_DEFAULT_VERSION_TAG`
    (default `unspecified`) when absent. Enable the header to tag a run.

  ## Response 202
  ```json
  { "job_id": "5f1c…" }
  ```

  ## Error codes
  - `400` — filename missing.
  - `401` — missing or invalid `X-API-Key`.
  - `503` — MinIO / Postgres unreachable on cold start.

  ## Notes
  - Large PDFs (~hundreds of MB) currently load fully into memory.
    Presigned uploads are a planned follow-up.
  - The Temporal workflow handles all of: parse → chunk → identifier
    canonicalisation → optional Russian translation → Milvus insert →
    canonical-entity inject (Neo4j) → LightRAG KG extraction →
    cross-chunk merge → entity resolution → property-graph build →
    finalize. Graph half is best-effort; status ends in
    `vector_only` if it gives up.

  ## Identifier canonicalisation

  During ingestion 19 deterministic identifier types are pulled out
  of the document text via regex + checksum-validated detectors and
  inserted into Neo4j as their own ``EntityNode``s before the LLM
  runs.  Each match is also written into the chunk's metadata
  (``canonical_identifiers``) and appended to ``node.text`` as a
  "Канонические идентификаторы:" block so the KG extractor sees the
  canonical form alongside the original mention.

  Types:

  | Group | Types |
  |-------|-------|
  | business | `PhoneNumber` (E.164), `Email`, `INN`, `OGRN`, `BIC`, `SNILS`, `ContractNumber`, `PostalAddress`, `DocumentDate`, `Amount` (RUB) |
  | digital  | `URL`, `Domain`, `TelegramHandle`, `VKProfile`, `TwitterHandle`, `InstagramHandle`, `LinkedInProfile`, `YouTubeChannel`, `GitHubProfile`, `UUID` |
  | device   | `IMEI` (Luhn), `MACAddress`, `LicensePlate` (RU directly + context-anchored generic), `VIN` (mod-11) |

  Overlap policy: when several detectors match overlapping spans
  (e.g. `URL` + `VKProfile` on `https://vk.com/user`), the
  specialised type wins.  See `_PRIORITY` in
  `src/ingestion/identifiers.py`.
}
